{
  "_comment": [
    "Hardware and site presets, shared by every host. Kinder serves this file verbatim",
    "from its presets route, so its shape is a contract, not an internal detail.",
    "",
    "Fragments are shaped like castor.schema itself (telescope, camera, environment.",
    "location, ...) rather than dotted-path strings, so a preset is a literal subset of",
    "the request a user would save or send.",
    "",
    "Telescopes and cameras are listed per profile rather than as one global catalogue:",
    "choosing a site is what narrows them, which is the reason the site selector sits",
    "above the others. They stay separate lists rather than fixed pairings because",
    "cameras do get moved between telescopes.",
    "",
    "A profile with an 'environment' block is a real observing site and applying it fills",
    "in the site's coordinates and sky. A profile without one is a hardware family only",
    "and touches nothing outside 'instrument' — deliberately, because inventing a location",
    "for a telescope model would silently produce wrong airmass and moon geometry.",
    "",
    "'median_seeing_fwhm' is a reference figure for display only and is never written into",
    "the form: seeing is a condition of the night being planned, not a property of the site,",
    "and it is the field an observer is most likely to have set deliberately.",
    "",
    "Filters are global. Bands are a property of the observation rather than of the site,",
    "and the standard sets are not tied to one telescope."
  ],

